        "original_id": "40637452-9b7c-516e-9a1c-ad4fc2afb6f3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen James Meridith Brown\n- Organizations: Central Catholic Library\n- Places: Holywood, County Down, Kilcrony, Wicklow, Belfast Lough, Belfast, Bangor\n- Roles: Jesuit priest, writer, bibliographer, librarian\n\nFacts:\n- Stephen James Meridith Brown was born on 24 September 1881 in Holywood, County Down, Ireland.\n- Holywood is a civil parish and townland of 755 acres on the shore of Belfast Lough between Belfast and Bangor.\n- Stephen Brown was an Irish Catholic Jesuit priest, writer, bibliographer, and librarian.\n- Stephen Brown founded the Central Catholic Library on 25 June 1922 to help the laity educate themselves.\n- Stephen James Meridith Brown died on 8 May 1962 in Kilcrony, Wicklow, Ireland.",
